{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Build an HTML fragment: a gallery of three product cards, each with a placeholder image, a title, and a price. Use placeholder images."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "<div class=\"gallery\">\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <img src=\"https://placehold.co/300x200?text=Product+A\" alt=\"Product A\" width=\"300\" height=\"200\">\n    <h3>Product A</h3>\n    <p>$19.99</p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <img src=\"https://placehold.co/300x200?text=Product+B\" alt=\"Product B\" width=\"300\" height=\"200\">\n    <h3>Product B</h3>\n    <p>$24.99</p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <img src=\"https://placehold.co/300x200?text=Product+C\" alt=\"Product C\" width=\"300\" height=\"200\">\n    <h3>Product C</h3>\n    <p>$29.99</p>\n  </div>\n</div>"}], "kind": "web", "lang": "HTML", "img": true}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Find some real images online for a hero banner about hiking and put them in an HTML section."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I can't fetch live images, so I've used placeholder images you can swap for real ones later (just replace each src). Here's the section:\n\n<section class=\"hero\">\n  <img src=\"https://placehold.co/1200x400?text=Hiking+Hero\" alt=\"Scenic hiking trail\" width=\"1200\" height=\"400\">\n  <h1>Explore the Trails</h1>\n  <p>Placeholder image above \u2014 replace the src with your own photo when ready.</p>\n</section>"}], "kind": "web", "lang": "HTML", "img": true}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Create an HTML fragment showing a blog post preview with a realistic placeholder photo, a headline, and a one-line excerpt."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "<article class=\"preview\">\n  <img src=\"https://picsum.photos/seed/blogpost/600/300\" alt=\"Article thumbnail\" width=\"600\" height=\"300\">\n  <h2>How We Cut Build Times in Half</h2>\n  <p>A short look at the caching change that made the difference.</p>\n</article>"}], "kind": "web", "lang": "HTML", "img": true}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Build a self-contained HTML fragment with an image placeholder that works offline (no external requests)."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "<figure class=\"offline-card\">\n  <img src=\"data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' width='600' height='400'><rect width='100%25' height='100%25' fill='%23223'/><text x='50%25' y='50%25' fill='%23fff' font-size='28' text-anchor='middle' dominant-baseline='middle'>No External Requests</text></svg>\" alt=\"Offline placeholder\" width=\"600\" height=\"400\">\n  <figcaption>This placeholder is an inline SVG \u2014 no network needed.</figcaption>\n</figure>"}], "kind": "web", "lang": "HTML", "img": true}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Give me an HTML avatar row: four circular placeholder avatars for a team page."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "<div class=\"team\">\n  <img class=\"avatar\" src=\"https://dummyimage.com/80x80/4a90d9/ffffff&text=AB\" alt=\"Team member AB\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\">\n  <img class=\"avatar\" src=\"https://dummyimage.com/80x80/50b96a/ffffff&text=CD\" alt=\"Team member CD\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\">\n  <img class=\"avatar\" src=\"https://dummyimage.com/80x80/d95c4a/ffffff&text=EF\" alt=\"Team member EF\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\">\n  <img class=\"avatar\" src=\"https://dummyimage.com/80x80/9b59b6/ffffff&text=GH\" alt=\"Team member GH\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\">\n</div>"}], "kind": "web", "lang": "HTML", "img": true}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Build a complete, self-contained HTML page that explains a 3-step process, each step illustrated with a labeled placeholder image."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n  <title>The Process</title>\n  <style>\n    body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 720px; margin: 2rem auto; }\n    .step { display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: center; margin: 1.5rem 0; }\n    .step img { border-radius: 8px; }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <h1>The Process</h1>\n  <section class=\"step\">\n    <img src=\"https://placehold.co/200x140?text=Step+1\" alt=\"Step 1: Prepare\" width=\"200\" height=\"140\">\n    <p><strong>Step 1 \u2014 Prepare.</strong> Gather everything you need before you start.</p>\n  </section>\n  <section class=\"step\">\n    <img src=\"https://placehold.co/200x140?text=Step+2\" alt=\"Step 2: Build\" width=\"200\" height=\"140\">\n    <p><strong>Step 2 \u2014 Build.</strong> Assemble the pieces in order.</p>\n  </section>\n  <section class=\"step\">\n    <img src=\"https://placehold.co/200x140?text=Step+3\" alt=\"Step 3: Review\" width=\"200\" height=\"140\">\n    <p><strong>Step 3 \u2014 Review.</strong> Check the result and refine.</p>\n  </section>\n</body>\n</html>"}], "kind": "web", "lang": "HTML", "img": true}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Search the web for pictures of golden retrievers and build a small HTML card with one."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Rather than searching (image search results aren't reliable to hotlink), I've used a placeholder you can replace with a real photo:\n\n<div class=\"pet-card\">\n  <img src=\"https://placehold.co/400x300?text=Golden+Retriever\" alt=\"Golden retriever\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\">\n  <h3>Golden Retriever</h3>\n  <p>Swap the image src for your own photo when you have one.</p>\n</div>"}], "kind": "web", "lang": "HTML", "img": true}
